        <ArticleTitle>Sequential versus combined initiation of disease-modifying therapy in HFrEF: a narrative review.</ArticleTitle>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText>Guideline-directed medical therapy for heart failure with reduced ejection fraction has historically been initiated sequentially, with each agent titrated to its maximum tolerated dose before the next is added. This review examines the pharmacological and trial-design reasons that convention arose and the emerging evidence that it delays benefit.</AbstractText>
